/OS/8 SYS & AUX HANDLER FOR SYKES 7200
/
/ORIGINAL BY M. PETERSON; MODIFICATIONS AND
/BOOTSTRAP BY P.M. HOLTHAM AND I.M. TEMPLETON
/AUX MODS BY I.M. TEMPLETON
/NATIONAL RESEARCH COUNCIL OF CANADA
/OTTAWA CANADA K1A 0R6
/
/THIS HANDLER PACKS AND UNPACKS STORED
/DATA TO INCREASE DISK CAPACITY BY 33% -
/4 12-BIT CORE WORDS ARE COMPRESSED
/INTO 6 8-BIT DISK WORDS WITH NO LOSS IN
/DATA TRANSFER RATE. THE STORAGE SYSTEM IS:
/WORD 1:	HIGH 1	HIGH 2
/WORD 2:	    LOW 1
/WORD 3:	    LOW 3
/WORD 4:	    LOW 2
/WORD 5:	HIGH 4	HIGH 3
/WORD 6:	    LOW 4
/
/N.B. STORAGE STARTS AT TRACK 0 SECTOR 1 OF DISK
/ALL DISK IS USED, IBM COMPATIBILITY LOST
/
/
/DEVICE CODE IS 32
/DEVICE TYPE IS 60
/
/SET BLOCK COUNT IN PIP TO 6546
/ (-666 DECIMAL) BY:
/	.GET SYS PIP
/	.ODT
/	13660/0000 6546
/	^C
/	.SAVE SYS PIP
/
/OPTIONAL RESORC PATCHES:
/	.GET SYS RESORC
/	.ODT
/	2300/0000 2331	/SY
/	2301/0000 1330	/KX
/	2302/0000 6546	/-666 DEC.
/	14467/0000 0614	/FL
/	14470/2405 1720	/OP
/	^C
/	.SAVE SYS RESORC
EJECT
